# What never enters the build context.
#
# The node-js buildpack packed the whole checkout, so every deploy compressed,
# pushed and pulled a multi-GB layer for a 48 second build. docs/ alone is
# 1.2G and reviews/ 450M and neither is read by `next build`. Keeping the
# context to the source the build actually compiles is most of the win.

.git
.github

# Never let a credential reach a layer. The app is configured by the platform
# at run time and `loadRootEnv()` is a no-op when the file is absent.
.env
.env.*

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.next-*
**/.next-*
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.pnpm-store

docs
reviews
context
.tmp
.vercel
.claude
.worktrees
supabase/.branches
supabase/.temp

*.zip
*.log
.DS_Store
